# Line endings are part of the product here, not a style preference.
#
# `rust-embed` bakes everything under assets/ into the binary VERBATIM. Without
# this file a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true by default on the GitHub
# runners) produces CRLF working-tree copies, so the Windows release binary ships
# assets that are byte-different from every other platform's. That breaks three
# things at once:
#   - the byte-compare writes 8sync relies on to leave user-edited files alone and
#     to keep omp's prompt-cache prefix stable;
#   - frontmatter/YAML parsing of the deployed rules, which matches on "\n" keys;
#   - shell installers and hooks, which must be LF to run at all.
#
# Normalise every text file to LF in the repo AND in the working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
